# Focus and keys (3-E2a). In a row, 100 px each: Save x 0..100, the
# note 100..200 (tabindex 0), Gone 200..300 (disabled), the aside
# 300..400 (tabindex -1), Cancel 400..500.
# Not `focus` and `blur`: Chromium also sends them to the window when
# focus leaves the page, and vapors has no window. `focusin` and
# `focusout` carry the same moves between elements; the order of all four
# is pinned by vapors-elements' focus tests.
cancel button#cancel
listen keydown keyup focusin focusout click pointerdown
key Tab                       to Save
expect focus button#save
key Tab                       to the note
expect focus div#note
key Tab                       past Gone and the aside, to Cancel
expect focus button#cancel
key Tab                       past the last: focus leaves the page
expect focus body
key Shift+Tab                 back from outside: the last, Cancel
expect focus button#cancel
key Enter                     clicks on keydown
expect event click button#cancel
key Space                     clicks on keyup
expect event click button#cancel
click 350 20                  a press on the aside focuses it
expect focus div#aside
key Tab                       from the aside (tabindex -1), on from its place: Cancel
expect focus button#cancel
click 250 20                  Gone is disabled: no click, and focus leaves Cancel
expect no event click
expect focus body
key x                         with nothing focused, keys go to the body
expect event keydown body
tap 50 20                     a tap on Save: focus moves to it, then its click
expect event click button#save
expect focus button#save
tap 450 20                    Cancel cancels its pointerdown: the click comes, focus stays
expect event click button#cancel
expect focus button#save
